# plistCSV project overview

Angular Full-Stack (generator v3.8) personal app: parse Flight Report **FlightIndex.plist** → **CSV** for pilot logbook import; optional monthly **F12 PDF** on the main route.

## Stack

- Client: AngularJS 1.x (`plistCsvApp`), ui-router, ui-bootstrap, angularMoment, Grunt build
- Server: Express 4, Sequelize 3, SQLite/PostgreSQL, **bplist-parser** on upload
- Runtime: Node **^12.22.12** — do not bump Node or major deps without approval

## Conventions

- Primary feature: `client/app/main/` + `server/api/workout/` (upload) + `server/api/airport/`
- API modules: `server/api/<name>/` with `index.js`, `*.controller.js`, `*.model.js`
- Register routers in `server/routes.js`
- Reference stack patterns in **`~/fraBering`** (read-only) for Node 12 and future Firebase

## Build & test

- Dev: `grunt serve` (use `nvm use`)
- Prod: `grunt build` then `npm start` from `dist/` when deploying built assets
- Tests: `npm test`

## Do not

- Upgrade Angular, Express, Sequelize, or Node major versions unprompted
- Replace Grunt/Bower without explicit request
- Edit fraBering when working on plistCSV unless Andy authorizes
